The company''s first product, launched in 2020, was the world''s first CBD-infused tampon, designed to provide localized relief from menstrual cramps. Building on this, Daye introduced a tampon-based at-home screening kit. This platform enables users to test for disruptions in the vaginal microbiome, which can indicate susceptibility to infections like bacterial vaginosis (BV) and yeast infections. The service has expanded to include screening for STIs such as chlamydia, gonorrhoea, and trichomonas, as well as HPV, using PCR technology for analysis in accredited labs. The business model operates on a direct-to-consumer basis, selling products like organic tampons, diagnostic kits, and supplements via its website, with options for monthly subscriptions. The company also provides personalized aftercare, including prescription treatments and consultations with healthcare specialists. 

Daye has raised approximately $18.6 million (£14 million) in funding through several rounds, including a Series A round of £10 million ($11.5 million) in October 2022. Key investors include Hambro Perks, MassMutual Ventures, Khosla Ventures, and Index Ventures. The company is preparing for expansion into the U.S. market and aims to develop a comprehensive digital health platform covering conditions like PCOS and endometriosis. 

Keywords: gynaecological health, femtech, at-home diagnostics, vaginal microbiome screening, STI testing, menstrual health, CBD tampons, period care, Valentina Milanova, women''s health research, digital health platform, telehealth, direct-to-consumer, venture capital, medical devices, HPV screening, personalized medicine, femcare, pelvic pain, subscription service', '["Health Platform","accelerator","data management","social media marketing software","static site generator","database","medical testing","online community software","sales","corporate learning management systems","Biotechnology","Gynaecological Health","help desk software","Venture Capital","web fonts","BioTechnology","editors","visual and user generated content marketing","predictive analytics","marketing","sales enablement","marketing automation","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","Good Health And Well-Being (#3)","Angel","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","Cannabis","content management system","other advertising software","Selling own inventory","marketing analytics","marketing performance measurement","software development","DT and LS","it infrastructure","customer data platforms","open source","database management","help desk management","tag management","email","team collaboration","widgets","web servers","online review management","customer service","Horizon Europe","uk is8 life sciences","programming languages","documentation tools","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","advertising","human resource","slush24","Manufacturing","Wellness Beauty","customer self-service","website builders","miscellaneous","programming","Personal Health","business intelligence","e-commerce","office suites","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","Medical Devices","intelligence and analytics","analytics","other audio-video-graphics software","devops","Sustainable Development Goals","issue trackers","science-based","document management systems","cad &