The core of the business is the "Gamebox," an interactive smart room designed for groups of two to six players. These rooms utilize a combination of projection mapping, touch-sensitive walls, 3D motion tracking, and surround sound to create immersive, shared adventures without the need for headsets. Players wear lightweight visors with tracking dots, allowing the system to follow their movements as they interact with the game projected on the 360-degree screens. The experience is designed to be collaborative, requiring teamwork to solve puzzles and complete challenges in 30-to-60-minute sessions. The target market is broad, encompassing families, couples on date nights, groups of friends, and corporate teams seeking team-building activities.

Revenue is generated through ticket sales for these gaming sessions, with prices around $30 per person for an hour. The company''s business model includes both company-owned venues and a franchise and concession model. This allows Immersive Gamebox to be integrated into existing entertainment centers, movie theaters, and malls. The firm has aggressively pursued global expansion, signing significant franchise deals to enter new markets. The company develops its game library in-house and through strategic IP partnerships with major entertainment studios like Netflix, Paramount, and Sony Pictures. This has led to the creation of popular games based on franchises such as "Squid Game," "Ghostbusters," "PAW Patrol," and "Angry Birds".

Keywords: social gaming, immersive entertainment, location-based entertainment, interactive gaming, franchise, projection mapping, motion tracking, group experiences, experiential retail, out-of-home entertainment', '["database","sales","Media","hris management","Venture Capital","web fonts","recruitment marketing","online form builders","marketing","marketing automation","customer relationship management","human resources","Angel","frameworks and libraries","content management system","other advertising software","online video platforms","marketing analytics","marketing performance measurement","it infrastructure","uk is8 creative industries","web platform extensions","tag management","widgets","search engines","content delivery network","programming languages","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","advertising","Pay Per Result","miscellaneous","programming","Ticketing","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","intelligence and analytics","video players","analytics","Leisure","Gaming","web analytics","platform as a service","visualisation software","b2c","Social","Digital Entertainment","font scripts","social networks","blogs","applicant tracking systems","design","tools","captcha","web tools and plugins","web hosting"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 79.72, 960, 0, 0, 49999980, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:39:10.020Z', 'GBP', '2021-06', 'Series A', 8333330);

The business operated as an online marketplace where customers could order a wide range of products, including fresh fruits, vegetables, meat, dairy, and ethically-sourced household goods, directly from a network of over 450 producers. Farmdrop''s model was designed to disintermediate the traditional supply chain, allowing farmers to receive a significantly larger share of the retail price—initially around 70-80%. Revenue was generated through a commission on each transaction, with the majority of the price going back to the producer. The service initially launched with a ''click and collect'' model at local hubs like pubs and community centres before transitioning to a direct-to-home delivery service using a fleet of electric vans. 

The platform provided logistical support, aggregating customer orders and coordinating delivery routes, allowing producers to focus on their craft. A key feature was that much of the produce was harvested to order, which minimized food waste compared to traditional retail. Over its lifespan, Farmdrop raised a total of $55.4M (£36M+) through multiple funding rounds from investors including Atomico, LGT Impact Ventures, and Belltown Ventures. Despite its ethical mission and significant backing, the company faced challenges in scaling its complex logistics and achieving profitability. After expanding its product range and delivery network, the company ultimately entered administration in December 2021, ceasing trading after failing to secure the necessary additional funding to continue operations. 

Keywords: online grocery, farm-to-table, ethical grocer, food delivery, local produce, sustainable farming, direct-to-consumer, food supply chain, e-commerce, social enterprise', '["personalization","data management","database","software as a service","hris management","Venture Capital","e-commerce platforms","web fonts","recruitment marketing","quality management systems","Food Logistics & Delivery","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","human resources","Angel","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","testing and qa","content management system","storage","digital asset management","other advertising software","enterprise","marketing analytics","data quality","Performance Management","Organic","web frameworks","customer data platforms","web platform extensions","tag management","advanced analytics and data science","widgets","web servers","search engines","software framework","customer service","content delivery network","programming languages","Commission","Breakout stage","advertising","infrastructure as a service","payment processing","error and exception monitoring","Manufacturing","web driver","enterprise resource planning","Pay Per Result","Farm Marketplace","miscellaneous","programming","caching","Groceries","cloud infrastructure computing","business intelligence","e-commerce","office suites","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","intelligence and analytics","real user monitoring","analytics","devops","operating systems & computing languages","cloud hosting","web analytics","a-b testing","b2c","javascript frameworks","Direct-to-Consumer","Marketplace & ecommerce","live chat","communications technology","font scripts","Producer","Crowdfunded","social networks","blogs","applicant tracking systems","tools","ui frameworks","accounting and finance","continuous integration","Food","containerization","operating systems","maps","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 79.14, 770, 0, 0, 