The company operates in the K-12 education market, directly serving schools and teachers. Its business model is based on providing a comprehensive curricular proposal that includes a wide array of resources. These resources range from manipulable materials for hands-on learning to digital platforms featuring interactive activities and games, complemented by detailed teacher training and support. Revenue is generated through subscriptions or licensing fees paid by educational institutions for access to this integrated system. 

Innovamat''s core offering is a structured pedagogical program that guides students through mathematical concepts in a scaffolded manner, starting with concrete manipulation, moving to pictorial representation, and finally to abstract symbols. The platform provides personalized learning paths, allowing students to progress at their own pace while enabling teachers to monitor progress and identify areas where intervention is needed. A key differentiator is its focus on problem-solving and critical thinking rather than rote learning, aiming to build a solid and lasting understanding of mathematics. The company has achieved significant milestones, including rapid expansion into various regions of Spain and entry into international markets such as Italy and several Latin American countries, serving thousands of schools and hundreds of thousands of students. 

