The app initially launched to help mothers connect with other local, like-minded women using a swipe-based mechanism. It has since expanded its scope to serve a broader female audience. In 2019, the company introduced a community for women trying to conceive. By 2021, it had added dedicated spaces for women navigating perimenopause and menopause. The platform allows users to join groups based on specific topics, interests, and life stages, such as due dates for expecting mothers. Key features include discussion forums, live audio conversations called "Pods," identity verification for safety, and content filters to mute potentially triggering topics. 

Peanut has secured significant funding from investors, including a $12 million Series A round in May 2020 led by EQT Ventures, which brought its total funding to $21.8 million at the time. Other key investors include Index Ventures and the Female Founders Fund. The business model is focused on community growth, with potential future monetization through premium features. The app is free to join and available on iOS and Android devices. 

Keywords: social network, women''s health, motherhood, pregnancy, fertility, menopause, community app, female founders, femtech, peer support, social discovery, online community, parenting, women''s wellness, new mothers, trying to conceive, perimenopause, mom friends, female connection, venture capital', '["Health Platform","corporate","accelerator","database","corporate learning management systems","Media","Venture Capital","editors","marketing","marketing automation","javascript graphics","Network Security","Good Health And Well-Being (#3)","Angel","frameworks and libraries","other advertising software","UKis Digital and technologies","DT and LS","web frameworks","uk is8 creative industries","Artificial Intelligence","tag management","team collaboration","widgets","web servers","Location Based","Digital Care","software framework","Hard Tech","content delivery network","programming languages","documentation tools","Fertility","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","advertising","human resource","Menopause","miscellaneous","programming","cloud infrastructure computing","Analytics","Parenting","Social media","javascript libraries","intelligence and analytics","containers","advertising networks","Network Management","real user monitoring","analytics","Leisure","devops","Gender Equality (#5)","Sustainable Development Goals","issue trackers","science-based","operating systems & computing languages","cloud hosting","web analytics","Femtech","platform as a service","uk is8 digital and technologies","Health","b2c","javascript frameworks","live chat","social networks","Tech for Patients","Mobile app","design","ui frameworks","Deep Tech","Machine Learning","machine learning","containerization","Woman Founder"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 68.03, 450000, 1, 1, 54545433, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:39:10.020Z', 'GBP', '2020-05', 'Series A', 9090905);
 
 The core of Smol''s business is a subscription-based service delivering concentrated, vegan, and cruelty-free laundry detergent capsules, dishwasher tablets, and other home cleaning products directly to consumers'' doors. This model allows the company to offer its products at a price point up to 50% lower than established brands. A key differentiator is the company''s commitment to reducing plastic waste; its primary packaging is plastic-free and recyclable, a significant departure from the bulky plastic containers common in the sector. The product formulations are another critical aspect, with a focus on high performance using fewer chemicals, demonstrated by their laundry capsules which are designed to be effective in both hot and cold washes. 
 
 Since its launch, Smol has expanded its product line to include fabric conditioner, multi-purpose surface sprays, and personal care items like shampoo and body bars, all adhering to the same principles of sustainability and convenience. The company has demonstrated significant market traction, having served over half a million customers and sold more than 100 million laundry capsules by late 2020. This growth trajectory was further validated when the company achieved B Corp certification in July 2022, legally committing it to high standards of social and environmental performance, transparency, and accountability. Keywords: direct-to-consumer, subscription service, eco-friendly cleaning, home care, plastic-free packaging, sustainable products, B Corp, vegan cleaning, concentrated formulas, cruelty-free', '["Venture Capital","web fonts","recruitment marketing","marketing automation","Angel","storage","other advertising software","Selling own inventory","online video platforms","marketing analytics","tag management","widgets","content delivery network","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","advertising","payment processing","error and exception monitoring","Manufacturing","Home Living","cloud infrastructure computing","e-commerce","hosting panels","javascript libraries","intelligence and analytics","video players","customer experience management","analytics","Responsible Consumption And Production (#12)","Sustainable Development Goals","Climate Tech","cloud hosting","web analytics","platform as a service","b2c","font scripts","social networks","applicant tracking systems","B Corp","Woman Founder","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","colt","vc_backed","funded"]', 79.12, 110000, 0, 0, 144000000, -1144427, 2022, -853415, 2024, '[{"year":2022,"revenue":25079629,"ebitda":-1144427,"profit":-1232660,"rnd":null,"valuation":144000000,"employees":68},{"year":2023,"revenue":31200000,"ebitda":-1144427,"profit":-5245890,"rnd":null,"valuation":144000000,"employees":83},{"year