The company primarily serves clients in the construction, mining, and rail industries, as well as those involved in managing civil infrastructure. These clients benefit from real-time data that helps them make informed decisions about the maintenance and safety of their assets.

Worldsensing operates in the global market, with a presence in 70 countries. Its business model revolves around selling its IoT devices and offering related software services. The company generates revenue through the sale of its hardware products (sensors and data loggers) and through subscription-based software services that provide data analytics and monitoring capabilities.

The company has been recognized for its commitment to sustainability, being listed among 100 companies embracing circular economy practices. This means they focus on reducing waste and making the most of resources, which is increasingly important in today''s business environment.

In summary, Worldsensing leverages IoT technology to provide critical monitoring solutions that enhance safety and efficiency in various industries. By offering both hardware and software solutions, the company ensures continuous monitoring and data-driven decision-making for its clients.

